# Normalise text files to LF in the index, whatever wrote them on disk.
#
# Without this, git stores exactly the bytes it is given (core.autocrlf is
# false here), so any tool that writes CRLF turns a small edit into a
# whole-file diff. That is not hypothetical: 23 source files were silently
# converted to CRLF by editing scripts before this was added, because Python's
# text mode translates "\n" to os.linesep on write. Scripts should still pass
# newline="" when writing tracked files, but this makes the repo immune either
# way rather than relying on everyone remembering.
#
# Binaries are detected automatically by `text=auto`, so images and the
# Ratehawk .zst dumps are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
